 "notes": [
  [
   "SAO++ power select: the switch common (VLOAD) feeds the AA light and the transistor. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell.",
   [
    38.1,
    30.48
   ]
  ],
  [
   "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other. D7 is the series cell diode docs/standard.md section 3 requires",
   [
    38.1,
    34.29
   ]
  ],
  [
   "(this board is wired to SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2): nothing can push current back into the CR2032.",
   [
    38.1,
    38.1
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Q1 = two P-channel MOSFETs (the maker's DMP3085LSD). SCL and SDA only touch the gates, through R7 / R8: an insulated input, so the bus cannot feed the board or the cell.",
   [
    38.1,
    41.91
   ]
  ],
  [
   "A light is on while its line is LOW: OH follows SCL, SD follows SDA. RTS (D4) and CTS (D5) are lit directly by the badge's GPIO1 / GPIO2 pins, about 1 mA each when high,",
   [
    38.1,
    45.72
   ]
  ],
  [
   "in every switch position (they never touch VLOAD). SYN (D6) is lit by whatever the user wires to pad TP1 (board-only bare pad, net SYN; no schematic symbol).",
   [
    38.1,
    49.53
   ]
  ],
  [
   "AA (D1) shows that the switched supply VLOAD is present. All six lights use the house 1.3 k resistor (the maker used 47 ohm).",
   [
    38.1,
    53.34
   ]
  ],
  [
   "R1, R2, R3 and R5 sit on the supply side of their LED so that, on the board, another track can pass between their pads (one copper layer, no vias).",
   [
    38.1,
    57.15
   ]
  ]
 ]
}